oduct. For two-dimensional vectors \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{w} = \\begin{pmatrix} w_1 \\\\ w_2 \\end{pmatrix}\\), the magnitude of the cross product is given by the absolute value of the determinant of the matrix formed by these vectors:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\left| v_1 w_2 - v_2 w_1 \\right|\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{w} = \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\left| (-7)(2) - (1)(5) \\right| = \\left| -14 - 5 \\right| = \\left| -19 \\right| = 19\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram is \\(\\boxed{19}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{19}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:160"}
